repository-code: "https://github.com/Urielledezma/Behavioural-Finance-Studies"
abstract: >-
  A series of studies in behavioural finance built on a common principle: a
  bias is injected into simulated investors at a strength fixed in advance, so
  that the estimators used on real brokerage data can be checked against a known
  ground truth. The first study, P01, injects the disposition effect and
  overprecision into synthetic trading records for eight scenarios and tests
  whether the proportion-of-gains-realised estimator and the turnover
  regression recover them, including two confounds under which the
  disposition estimator fires with no bias present.
keywords:
  - behavioural finance
  - disposition effect
  - overconfidence
  - agent-based simulation
  - Monte Carlo
  - bootstrap
  - Python
